product-rating (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The header no longer cuts off the account name on a narrow screen. The
    label and the name may now sit on two lines, and the name is shortened
    only when it is too long for a line of its own.
  * The rating scale closes with the number of the top rating, the way it
    opens with a zero. Both rows the scale wraps into on a phone are the
    same length, and a tap on that number gives the full ten stars.
  * No change to the installation layout, to the configuration or to the
    database.

 -- roemer2201 <roemer2201@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

product-rating (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New app mark: a barcode above a row of five stars on a green ground. It
    replaces the blue star and barcode symbol in the browser tab, in the web
    app manifest and on the iOS home screen.
  * Icons already on a home screen are only picked up when the app is added
    again; the browser tab shows the new one after the next reload.
  * No change to the installation layout, to the configuration or to the
    database.

 -- roemer2201 <roemer2201@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

product-rating (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A capture put into the offline queue survives the app being killed. On
    iOS, swiping the app out of the app switcher ends the process at once,
    and a write that had been reported as done but not yet committed went
    with it - the interface counted a capture that was nowhere on disk.
  * The queue now asks to have its storage treated as persistent, so the
    browser does not discard it when the device runs short of space or the
    app goes unused for a week.
  * No change to the installation layout or to the configuration.

 -- roemer2201 <roemer2201@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0000

product-rating (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Accounts carry a display name beside the username: the name the rest of
    the household sees at a rating, a price or a trash entry. Everybody sets
    and changes their own; the username stays the identifier used to log in.
  * New database migration 0008 adds the nullable column users.display_name.
    It runs on its own during the upgrade, like every migration before it.
  * New CLI subcommand "product-rating user display-name USERNAME [NAME]",
    plus --display-name for "user add" and a column in "user list".
  * Export and import carry the display name along; older export files
    without the field are still read.
  * "proxy-config --server apache" resolves again; the canonical name was
    missing from the alias table while help and README used it.
  * Two captures written in the same millisecond keep their order in the
    offline queue instead of falling back to the order of their keys.
  * No change to the installation layout or to the configuration.

 -- roemer2201 <roemer2201@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

product-rating (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First released version. Versions follow semantic versioning; the entry
    here has to match the version in package.json, which build-deb.sh reads.
  * The application now sets its own hardening headers, including the
    Content-Security-Policy. The shipped proxy examples only add HSTS.
  * No change to the installation layout, the configuration or the database
    schema compared to 0.0.0.

 -- roemer2201 <roemer2201@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

product-rating (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging (M11). Installs the API server and the built web
    client below /opt/product-rating, served by one process.
  * Adds a hardened systemd unit, a logrotate rule and the
    /usr/bin/product-rating wrapper for serve, migrate and fsck.
  * postinst creates the system user, the data directories and the session
    secret and applies the database migrations; purge asks before it
    removes the database and the photos.

 -- roemer2201 <roemer2201@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
